{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888570,"nonce":"aosvEcw1Rtp3B3RKD8VEZS6DkA0=","title":"A vmalert generatorURL carries no expression, so with FollowGeneratorURL set oto still cannot find the vmalert that evaluated the rule, and the vmui link form loses the expression it does carry","message":"**What is wrong.** vmalert's default generatorURL is `\u003cexternal.url\u003e/vmalert/alert?group_id=\u003cid\u003e\u0026alert_id=\u003cid\u003e` — no `g0.expr`. `ResolveRule` (`internal/sources/service/service.go:285`) derives the rules-API override from `rulematch.ParseGeneratorURL(...).ExternalURL` only when the parse succeeds (`service.go:301`), and the parse fails with `rulematch_generator_url_no_expr`, so even an operator who opted into `FollowGeneratorURL` gets no lookup unless the source has its own `prometheus_url`. Separately, the documented vmui override `-external.alert.source='vmui/#/?g0.expr={{.Expr|queryEscape}}'` puts the expression in a fragment that reads `/?g0.expr=…`; `url.ParseQuery` yields the key `/?g0.expr`, and `exprParamRe` (`^g(\\d+)\\.expr$`, `internal/sources/rulematch/generatorurl.go`) rejects it.\n\n**The demonstration.** Table inputs: `http://vmalert:8880/vmalert/alert?group_id=1036955090143761274\u0026alert_id=1074584496268461589` (vmalert docs example) and `http://vmui:8428/vmui/#/?g0.expr=up%20%3D%3D%200`. The first yields no override under `FollowGeneratorURL`; the second yields no expression.\n\n**Why it matters.** RuleSnapshots are the differentiator; vmalert users get the weakest version silently.\n\n**Where.** `generatorurl.go`: fragment parsing tolerates a hash-router prefix (`/?`), which is a genuine expression recovery and so a success. A separate, additive helper recognises the `/vmalert/alert` path and returns the vmalert root; `ParseGeneratorURL`'s meaning is unchanged — success still means an expression was recovered, and the vmalert form still returns `no_expr`. `service.go`'s `FollowGeneratorURL` branch uses the helper's root when the parse yields none. Following stays opt-in.\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** The vmui hash form parses with `VariantFragment` and the right expression; the default vmalert form still fails `ParseGeneratorURL` with `no_expr`, and with `FollowGeneratorURL` set `ResolveRule` queries the vmalert root's rules API; with `FollowGeneratorURL` unset nothing new is queried; existing Prometheus goldens unchanged.\n\n**Blocked by.** None — can start immediately.\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}